id: pm-gh1424
title: "GH-1424: Wait safely for contended Git merge-driver configuration"
description: Parallel package prepare hooks race on Git config.lock; SDK merge installation must wait for transient contention and preserve bounded actionable refusal for permanent failures.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T17:18:38.064Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:35.115Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:34.332Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:34.332Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Released Git config locks permit complete installation without caller retries; persistent locks fail within a declared bound without publishing a new attributes fence; non-contention failures are not retried; unchanged driver definitions are not rewritten; linked-worktree configuration migration remains isolated and race-safe
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub #1424
severity: medium
repro_steps: Hold .git/config.lock while starting parallel installed prepare hooks; release it after 200ms. Pre-fix installs fail with merge_git_config_unwritable instead of waiting.
resolution: "Coordinated installations across a clone's worktrees, read the selected configuration layer and skip identical definitions. Required native Git writes retry only lock contention with bounded backoff; persistent locks and other failures preserve typed refusal and attributes safety."
expected_result: "Concurrent merge setup succeeds after transient native lock release, avoids rewriting matching definitions, and never deletes external locks or publishes attributes after config failure."
actual_result: "Both linked merge suites passed 27 real Git cases, including concurrent installs, external native lock release, persistent lock refusal, malformed-config read/write race, idempotent bytes/mtime and worktree isolation. Actual packed SDK concurrent setup passed npm and Bun; full suite exact four-metric coverage passed."
component: SDK merge-driver installation
customer_impact: Parallel npm/Bun package prepare hooks can fail despite valid writable repositories.
